191
00:14:12,153 --> 00:14:15,875
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you're seated now, and you're mindful that you're seated, and now you drift off.

192
00:14:17,916 --> 00:14:21,177
[SPEAKER_00]: But if, at any point, you'll feel drifted off, I ask you,

193
00:14:22,468 --> 00:14:23,109
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you sitting?

194
00:14:23,829 --> 00:14:25,210
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you sitting or are you seated?

195
00:14:25,751 --> 00:14:26,391
[SPEAKER_00]: You would say yes.

196
00:14:28,573 --> 00:14:33,798
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the knowledge of the body position pertains to the body and it's there with the body.

197
00:14:35,419 --> 00:14:40,583
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why you can afford to forget it, in that mental keeping it in front of me all the time sense.

198
00:14:42,825 --> 00:14:43,286
[SPEAKER_00]: It takes time.

199
00:14:43,306 --> 00:14:50,452
[SPEAKER_00]: It's basically recognizing the peripheral to the extent necessary that things don't

200
00:14:51,780 --> 00:15:00,044
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, to the extent necessary that forgetting particular things doesn't induce general non-mindfulness.

201
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:01,945
[SPEAKER_00]: You can put it like that.

202
00:15:06,388 --> 00:15:14,312
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you might have lost a particular thought that I am seated here now, but you are still seated here now.

203
00:15:15,393 --> 00:15:15,773
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means,

204
00:15:16,812 --> 00:15:21,477
[SPEAKER_00]: Even when you were thinking, I'm seated here now, that wasn't your mindfulness.

205
00:15:21,877 --> 00:15:27,423
[SPEAKER_00]: The fact that you were seated right there and then, that's where your mindfulness was, or could have been.

206
00:15:38,694 --> 00:15:39,214
[SPEAKER_01]: You see, right?

207
00:15:39,274 --> 00:15:39,555
[SPEAKER_01]: If I...

208
00:15:40,714 --> 00:15:46,858
[SPEAKER_01]: From time to time in the day, I say, I sit down and I do something specific meditation, mindfulness of breathing.

209
00:15:48,559 --> 00:15:51,581
[SPEAKER_01]: I say, well, I will, I keep that in mind.

210
00:15:52,281 --> 00:15:53,462
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll be mindful of my breathing.

211
00:15:56,144 --> 00:15:57,925
[SPEAKER_01]: And I sit there for a while, but then I get up.

212
00:15:59,086 --> 00:16:00,407
[SPEAKER_01]: I think about this, think about that.

213
00:16:02,828 --> 00:16:05,770
[SPEAKER_01]: Then I might say, I'll be mindful of my body posture.

214
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:08,592
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll be mindful of my feelings.

215
00:16:09,292 --> 00:16:10,193
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll be mindful of this.

216
00:16:10,633 --> 00:16:12,734
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, am I...

217
00:16:13,334 --> 00:16:19,137
[SPEAKER_01]: I feel that I'm aware of my situation, my surroundings, the state of my mind.

218
00:16:20,658 --> 00:16:21,559
[SPEAKER_01]: But then I have doubt.

219
00:16:21,739 --> 00:16:24,020
[SPEAKER_00]: Am I actually being mindful of that particular thing?

220
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:26,201
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

221
00:16:26,221 --> 00:16:35,106
[SPEAKER_00]: Because I... Well, because you have to find your bodily posture, your breathing, your feelings, whatever you want to be mindful of.

222
00:16:35,646 --> 00:16:39,528
[SPEAKER_00]: You have to find that within the general situation.

223
00:16:40,157 --> 00:16:40,878
[SPEAKER_00]: Not in front of it.

224
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:48,284
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in that general situation, that's... that's how you have to start.

225
00:16:48,824 --> 00:16:56,090
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, within that, without abandoning the... the image of general situation, you have to start discerning feeling.

226
00:16:56,830 --> 00:16:59,092
[SPEAKER_00]: You have to start discerning presence of the body.

227
00:16:59,633 --> 00:17:02,935
[SPEAKER_01]: In this general situation, if I, eh...

228
00:17:04,577 --> 00:17:06,178
[SPEAKER_01]: I... yeah, I feel like in a...

229
00:17:06,258 --> 00:17:06,558
[SPEAKER_01]: I can...

230
00:17:07,119 --> 00:17:08,600
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm aware of the general situation, but

231
00:17:11,302 --> 00:17:13,103
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm surrounded by it, in a way.

232
00:17:13,383 --> 00:17:13,643
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

233
00:17:14,023 --> 00:17:14,563
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm within it.

234
00:17:14,684 --> 00:17:15,684
[SPEAKER_00]: It's empowered, yeah.

235
00:17:15,984 --> 00:17:26,149
[SPEAKER_01]: And whatever I think of as the body, within that, that stands for the body.

236
00:17:27,489 --> 00:17:27,949
[SPEAKER_00]: Pretty much.

237
00:17:28,710 --> 00:17:30,951
[SPEAKER_01]: And there can be a number of things.

238
00:17:30,971 --> 00:17:31,171
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

239
00:17:32,031 --> 00:17:35,733
[SPEAKER_00]: That will all be... inseparable from a body.

240
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:37,840
[SPEAKER_01]: It's conceivable.

241
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:46,484
[SPEAKER_01]: It'll be a thought, but always within the general... George, have a thought of general situation.

242
00:17:47,284 --> 00:17:50,445
[SPEAKER_01]: But if I do have a thought of general situation, is that not making it in front of me?

243
00:17:51,385 --> 00:17:51,846
[SPEAKER_00]: It depends.

244
00:17:52,526 --> 00:17:52,886
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

245
00:17:57,548 --> 00:18:00,969
[SPEAKER_00]: Whether it's going to be in front of you or not, it depends how you attend it.

246
00:18:01,109 --> 00:18:04,010
[SPEAKER_00]: If you over-attend it, under-attend it, miss-attend it.

247
00:18:04,770 --> 00:18:05,931
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't attend it properly...

248
00:18:07,428 --> 00:18:08,168
[SPEAKER_01]: General situation.

249
00:18:08,288 --> 00:18:09,688
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that's okay.

250
00:18:09,809 --> 00:18:10,629
[SPEAKER_00]: You can think behind you.

251
00:18:11,409 --> 00:18:15,410
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, if you're behind me, that can become in front of you.

252
00:18:16,670 --> 00:18:18,190
[SPEAKER_01]: Because must my mind be split?

253
00:18:19,071 --> 00:18:21,091
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it doesn't really matter that much, actually.

254
00:18:21,251 --> 00:18:24,992
[SPEAKER_00]: What matters is to develop the sense of the mindfulness of while.

255
00:18:26,712 --> 00:18:30,073
[SPEAKER_00]: The two simultaneous layers, if you want to put it that way.

256
00:18:32,733 --> 00:18:33,074
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

257
00:18:33,974 --> 00:18:34,914
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, particularly.

258
00:18:35,346 --> 00:18:39,107
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, the particular is that, or the bodily and mental.

259
00:18:39,487 --> 00:18:40,968
[SPEAKER_00]: You can put it as crudely as that.

260
00:18:43,188 --> 00:18:49,510
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, obviously, both bodily and mental are mental, in a certain way.

261
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:54,751
[SPEAKER_00]: But there are mental things that pertain solely to mental, and there are mental things to the bodily.

262
00:18:56,372 --> 00:18:59,953
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, mental is split into bodily and mental.

263
00:19:01,698 --> 00:19:04,521
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in that sense, everything is... your mind comes first.

264
00:19:04,641 --> 00:19:06,162
[SPEAKER_00]: Just without mind, it's inconceivable.

265
00:19:06,503 --> 00:19:08,885
[SPEAKER_00]: But not everything is entirely mental.

266
00:19:11,407 --> 00:19:18,954
[SPEAKER_00]: But even the whole thing of body and mind will not be able to stand if there is no body that is conscious out there, but everyone in the world.

267
00:19:26,722 --> 00:19:26,982
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

268
00:19:28,924 --> 00:19:33,105
[SPEAKER_01]: Or as you probably say this, the Pali word for situation is vipassana.

269
00:19:33,125 --> 00:19:36,346
[SPEAKER_00]: Vipassana.

270
00:19:37,867 --> 00:19:40,848
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's, eh... Yeah, I suppose.

271
00:19:41,108 --> 00:19:43,008
[SPEAKER_00]: But you have to start from the state of puthujjana.

272
00:19:43,669 --> 00:19:48,650
[SPEAKER_00]: So, being contacted, having things manifested, that would be the original situation.

273
00:19:50,071 --> 00:19:57,573
[SPEAKER_00]: By recognizing the original situation, you can eventually go through it, literally, discern through it,

274
00:19:59,046 --> 00:20:00,647
[SPEAKER_00]: Not left, right, above, below.

275
00:20:00,687 --> 00:20:01,327
[SPEAKER_00]: Right through it.

276
00:20:02,108 --> 00:20:04,189
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how you cease to regard it as mine.

277
00:20:05,690 --> 00:20:06,851
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then you're not contacted.

278
00:20:08,092 --> 00:20:09,273
[SPEAKER_01]: But there's still arising.

279
00:20:09,313 --> 00:20:09,593
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

280
00:20:09,693 --> 00:20:11,794
[SPEAKER_00]: So, puthujjana situation is taunted.

281
00:20:12,655 --> 00:20:14,416
[SPEAKER_00]: But situation will pretend to arising.

282
00:20:15,516 --> 00:20:17,438
[SPEAKER_00]: Arising in passing away of the five aggregates.

283
00:20:19,939 --> 00:20:23,281
[SPEAKER_00]: But if that touches you, if you make it mine, then you're contacted by it.

284
00:20:24,022 --> 00:20:25,663
[SPEAKER_00]: If it doesn't, then you're not.

285
00:20:29,337 --> 00:20:38,281
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, if the situation, general situation, you said that, that's... About this, before I forget it, because I forgot it once, I want to say.

286
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:47,746
[SPEAKER_00]: You can induce the mindfulness of a general situation.

287
00:20:48,506 --> 00:20:51,447
[SPEAKER_00]: And while you're mindful of the general situation, let your body do things.

288
00:20:52,948 --> 00:20:54,269
[SPEAKER_00]: Walk, sit, move about.

289
00:20:55,489 --> 00:20:57,010
[SPEAKER_00]: While you're mindful of the general situation,

290
00:20:59,854 --> 00:21:10,139
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that indirect way of seeing that body, not directly doing it, but letting it do, while you're looking at it through the mindful general situation, is one among the bodies.

291
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:13,380
[SPEAKER_00]: One among the experience of the bodies.

292
00:21:14,361 --> 00:21:15,582
[SPEAKER_01]: Every mindful of the body.

293
00:21:15,782 --> 00:21:15,962
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

294
00:21:16,902 --> 00:21:18,483
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the whole point of ānāpānasati.

295
00:21:19,043 --> 00:21:28,968
[SPEAKER_00]: Through doing breath, you do other things through this thing, which means they'll never be directly done,

296
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:32,101
[SPEAKER_00]: They'll be indirectly observed while they're done.

297
00:21:35,003 --> 00:21:42,186
[SPEAKER_00]: And what you feel there, what you perceive there, what you do there, is a feeling, is a perception, is something that's well done.

298
00:21:45,148 --> 00:21:51,931
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you have to start recognizing that indirectly, peripherally, seeing something remotely, still stands for that thing that you're seeing remotely.

299
00:21:52,312 --> 00:21:53,632
[SPEAKER_00]: Not just directly in front of you.

300
00:21:54,893 --> 00:21:56,094
[SPEAKER_00]: That's how mindfulness develops.

301
00:21:56,534 --> 00:21:58,435
[SPEAKER_00]: So, while you're mindful of the entire situation,

302
00:21:59,507 --> 00:22:09,594
[SPEAKER_00]: Your body is seated there on its own, almost as if it has its own existence, independent of you and your general situation, so to speak, not entirely.

303
00:22:10,374 --> 00:22:15,118
[SPEAKER_00]: But in a way, yes, because you don't have to be sitting to be seated.

304
00:22:15,138 --> 00:22:15,658
[SPEAKER_00]: You're seated.

305
00:22:16,519 --> 00:22:20,141
[SPEAKER_00]: But there is something the body does, yet you don't have to keep doing it.

306
00:22:20,181 --> 00:22:20,902
[SPEAKER_00]: Same with breathing.

307
00:22:22,102 --> 00:22:25,965
[SPEAKER_00]: You can be doing the breathing, but the body is also doing the breathing.

308
00:22:27,827 --> 00:22:28,808
[SPEAKER_00]: So you can be mindful of that.

309
00:22:28,828 --> 00:22:31,469
[SPEAKER_00]: Breathing as well, while you're mindful of the general situation.

310
00:22:33,050 --> 00:22:42,676
[SPEAKER_00]: So that... As if, like, because you're mindful of the general situation, you cannot be fully absorbed 100% into breathing or sitting or whatever else.

311
00:22:42,816 --> 00:22:44,417
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the whole point.

312
00:22:44,437 --> 00:22:45,077
[SPEAKER_00]: To not be.

313
00:22:45,697 --> 00:22:48,799
[SPEAKER_00]: Because then you start recognizing it indirectly, peripherally.

314
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:53,682
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is, again, the reason why this whole vipassana mainstream is completely wrong.

315
00:22:55,630 --> 00:23:00,353
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, they believe you can have a hundred percent attention upon the one thing, and you can't.

316
00:23:00,653 --> 00:23:01,733
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why the frustration...

317
00:23:01,753 --> 00:23:05,955
[SPEAKER_01]: I think I'm trying... like I said, your mind has to be split, but I'm trying to give a hundred percent to both.

318
00:23:06,396 --> 00:23:07,316
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, exactly.

319
00:23:07,356 --> 00:23:07,596
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

320
00:23:07,836 --> 00:23:11,478
[SPEAKER_00]: Your mind can be split, and then you can be trying to attend that hundred percent.

321
00:23:11,558 --> 00:23:12,258
[SPEAKER_00]: It's impossible.

322
00:23:13,639 --> 00:23:19,842
[SPEAKER_00]: Because of all of the different... because of peripheral in general, and infinity on that structure, you can't have one thing.

323
00:23:21,610 --> 00:23:27,812
[SPEAKER_00]: Or rather, that structure is one thing, but you can't step outside of it, and then attend it as one thing.

324
00:23:27,872 --> 00:23:28,633
[SPEAKER_00]: It's impossible.

325
00:23:28,773 --> 00:23:33,735
[SPEAKER_00]: You can only see it from within, which means it will always be nāma and rūpa.

326
00:23:36,736 --> 00:23:37,896
[SPEAKER_01]: Let me see one more.

327
00:23:37,916 --> 00:23:47,500
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the general situation, being mindful, being aware of it, and particularly those body and feelings,

328
00:23:50,241 --> 00:23:58,025
[SPEAKER_01]: And that awareness of the mindfulness, that's within that situation.

329
00:23:58,785 --> 00:23:59,065
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

330
00:23:59,405 --> 00:23:59,745
[SPEAKER_01]: As well.

331
00:23:59,926 --> 00:24:00,166
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

332
00:24:02,687 --> 00:24:02,967
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is...

333
00:24:02,987 --> 00:24:10,050
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is why, if you do it long enough, the belief that you can be outside of that situation will fade.

334
00:24:12,051 --> 00:24:13,632
[SPEAKER_00]: And that belief is sakāyabhid.

335
00:24:15,081 --> 00:24:18,223
[SPEAKER_00]: Whereby your sense of self, your personality, is outside of your experience.

336
00:24:18,243 --> 00:24:19,024
[SPEAKER_00]: You're just assuming.

337
00:24:19,644 --> 00:24:22,166
[SPEAKER_00]: Failing to see that that assumption is within this experience.

338
00:24:23,807 --> 00:24:40,118
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you keep seeing the situation in general, the entire situation, within that, while your mindful situation, in my body, of what you feel or whatever, partially, because you don't want to be fully absorbing what you feel, because you forget about the situation,

339
00:24:41,803 --> 00:24:46,224
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, it becomes apparent that, well, whatever arises within this, will be within this situation.

340
00:24:47,025 --> 00:24:51,466
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you do it long enough, you stop assuming that there can be anything out of the situation.

341
00:24:52,787 --> 00:24:54,447
[SPEAKER_01]: Because even your assumption is wrong.

342
00:24:54,907 --> 00:24:55,187
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

343
00:24:55,287 --> 00:24:56,968
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever it is, about it.

344
00:25:03,245 --> 00:25:10,889
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is how the sense of self is then recognized peripherally, ambiguously, within that situation, as a phenomenon.

345
00:25:11,250 --> 00:25:15,792
[SPEAKER_00]: And if it's within that situation, it cannot be the owner of that situation, cannot be the creator, cannot be the master.

346
00:25:17,853 --> 00:25:24,237
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you abandon ātavāda like that, which is the belief that your self is far more superior than your whole experience.

347
00:25:30,322 --> 00:25:35,234
[SPEAKER_00]: But if it's manifested, it's impermanent for a very reason.

348
00:25:35,816 --> 00:25:38,182
[SPEAKER_00]: And now you see it manifested, means it persists.

349
00:25:49,078 --> 00:25:51,699
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you're mindful of the situation...

350
00:25:51,759 --> 00:25:55,021
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll stop saying situation as general, because every situation is general.

351
00:25:55,601 --> 00:26:04,506
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you're mindful of the situation, and then within that mindfulness of the situation, keep a peripheral eye on what your body is doing.

352
00:26:06,707 --> 00:26:13,571
[SPEAKER_00]: There won't be anything left out, because whatever arises will be between the two, and that's already included in it.

353
00:26:16,736 --> 00:26:25,443
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you get used to that, or rather if you develop it to the insufficient extent, then you can also see that they're mutually determining each other.

354
00:26:26,244 --> 00:26:37,112
[SPEAKER_00]: Your entire situation would not be manifested if this random body is still not alive, sitting on the chair, breathing, being nurtured by food or whatever else.

355
00:26:39,154 --> 00:26:39,895
[SPEAKER_00]: And vice versa.

356
00:26:40,976 --> 00:26:46,380
[SPEAKER_00]: If there is no situation recognized as such, this body will not be manifested at all within.

357
00:26:50,701 --> 00:26:52,401
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you can't even imagine.

358
00:26:52,441 --> 00:26:53,102
[SPEAKER_00]: Inconceivable.

359
00:26:53,162 --> 00:26:54,602
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, inconceivable.

360
00:26:55,042 --> 00:26:56,202
[SPEAKER_00]: Every... like, that's the thing.

361
00:26:56,982 --> 00:26:59,163
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, thinking that that's already the situation.

362
00:27:01,923 --> 00:27:05,504
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's there.

363
00:27:10,485 --> 00:27:12,905
[SPEAKER_01]: When I was... in terms of the breath, when I was what?

364
00:27:12,925 --> 00:27:20,347
[SPEAKER_01]: When I was, say, attending to the breath, and I tried to attend to that as much as I can,

365
00:27:24,925 --> 00:27:28,188
[SPEAKER_01]: I think you wrote it in your notes on meditation.

366
00:27:28,889 --> 00:27:43,541
[SPEAKER_01]: You just said now, you allow the body and the feelings to arise by themselves, so to speak, to emerge or arise by themselves, so that you don't have to conceive it.

367
00:27:46,122 --> 00:27:49,123
[SPEAKER_01]: So, they're no longer conceived, they just arise as they do.

368
00:27:49,503 --> 00:27:54,926
[SPEAKER_00]: You recognize they would arise with whether you conceive them or not, which means my conceiving becomes redundant.

369
00:27:56,686 --> 00:28:05,850
[SPEAKER_01]: See, if I'm looking at the... if I'm doing ānāpānasati, like that, or breathing, breathing, breathing, and I'm...

370
00:28:05,910 --> 00:28:06,790
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm looking at the body.

371
00:28:08,731 --> 00:28:13,213
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the body arises and I'm like, oh, that's the body, which I'm not supposed to conceive.

372
00:28:15,502 --> 00:28:22,572
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, again, you don't conceive it necessarily just by thinking that.

373
00:28:22,913 --> 00:28:26,398
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, as I said, well, if you do ānāpānasati,

374
00:28:27,928 --> 00:28:30,129
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness of breathing is your situation.

375
00:28:30,969 --> 00:28:31,650
[SPEAKER_00]: I am breathing.

376
00:28:32,590 --> 00:28:33,591
[SPEAKER_00]: That's your situation.

377
00:28:34,191 --> 00:28:38,013
[SPEAKER_00]: Within that, I'm breathing while the body is like this.

378
00:28:38,293 --> 00:28:39,853
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm breathing while the body is like that.

379
00:28:40,314 --> 00:28:42,475
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm going to breathe in while the body will be like this.

380
00:28:42,555 --> 00:28:43,515
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm going to breathe...

381
00:28:43,535 --> 00:28:44,856
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm going to breathe feeling this.

382
00:28:44,936 --> 00:28:46,096
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm going to breathe feeling that.

383
00:28:46,637 --> 00:28:47,357
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the whole point.

384
00:28:48,898 --> 00:29:00,324
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you start thinking about the feeling and everything, you can't afford that, if your mindfulness gets developed to such an extent whereby an act of breathing, whether you do it or not, is where it's anchored.

385
00:29:01,524 --> 00:29:02,505
[SPEAKER_00]: And you are still breathing.

386
00:29:04,606 --> 00:29:11,069
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, when you go back to the breathing, you go back as if it was always there, because it was always there.

387
00:29:12,129 --> 00:29:17,652
[SPEAKER_00]: So, your forgetting becomes mind... well, rather, your forgetting becomes within the mindfulness.

388
00:29:19,661 --> 00:29:23,263
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you remember, everything is rendered as mindful memory.

389
00:29:26,305 --> 00:29:29,988
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindful memory means a memory that will not induce a vision.

390
00:29:30,008 --> 00:29:30,128
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

391
00:29:35,732 --> 00:29:41,035
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you mean, not induce a vision?

392
00:29:41,215 --> 00:29:48,660
[SPEAKER_00]: Not, eh... Well, like, an arahant can remember stuff he'd done when he was a contingent.

393
00:29:50,067 --> 00:29:53,589
[SPEAKER_00]: But none of those memories will induce a regeneration.

394
00:29:59,533 --> 00:30:13,402
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you forget about the breathing, but then you become mindful of the fact... well, when your body is mindful, but the breathing is still happening, even if you go and think about other things, when you get back to...

395
00:30:14,278 --> 00:30:15,439
[SPEAKER_00]: Or rather, let's put it like this.

396
00:30:15,999 --> 00:30:27,189
[SPEAKER_00]: Remembering that you were supposed to be breathing, practicing mindfulness of breathing, that act won't be like, oh, I remember something I forgot.

397
00:30:27,209 --> 00:30:35,215
[SPEAKER_00]: Remembering will just mean bringing you back to the breathing that is already there, and was already there, and was happening all this time.

398
00:30:35,775 --> 00:30:40,619
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, your mindfulness was already there, was already there, and was happening all this time.

399
00:30:42,490 --> 00:30:50,056
[SPEAKER_00]: So, remembering and forgetting doesn't induce a vijā anymore in regard to where was I, what was I doing, how to start again.

400
00:30:51,317 --> 00:30:55,160
[SPEAKER_00]: It just means going somewhere else and coming back to the other thing.

401
00:30:57,442 --> 00:30:58,583
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is what you do all the time.

402
00:30:59,143 --> 00:30:59,944
[SPEAKER_00]: But you don't know that.

403
00:31:01,105 --> 00:31:02,786
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you go somewhere else, you forget.

404
00:31:04,908 --> 00:31:05,188
[SPEAKER_00]: i.e.

405
00:31:05,468 --> 00:31:10,632
[SPEAKER_00]: the assumptions of a vijā and everything else, the upādāna, the perpetuate.

406
00:31:26,374 --> 00:31:35,000
[SPEAKER_01]: You can also start from dead breathing, looking at the situation inside.

407
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:35,781
[SPEAKER_00]: Satipaṭṭhāna.

408
00:31:36,021 --> 00:31:36,901
[SPEAKER_00]: Just take any of it.

409
00:31:38,342 --> 00:31:39,403
[SPEAKER_00]: You can start with any of it.

410
00:31:40,204 --> 00:31:42,706
[SPEAKER_00]: Either the body's here...

411
00:31:42,746 --> 00:31:45,107
[SPEAKER_00]: But there's so many different types of practicing body markets.

412
00:31:46,088 --> 00:31:47,129
[SPEAKER_00]: Looking at dead corpses.

413
00:31:48,532 --> 00:31:49,573
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a form of satipaṭṭhāna.

414
00:31:50,333 --> 00:31:50,533
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

415
00:31:50,573 --> 00:32:05,523
[SPEAKER_00]: Because a corpse, a corpse in regard to which you feel no loss, you feel dispassion, can be conceived without standing for a body.

416
00:32:06,503 --> 00:32:11,006
[SPEAKER_00]: Mind, body of others, body of both, internal, external, internal and external.

417
00:32:11,226 --> 00:32:13,027
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't, because it's entirely bodily.

418
00:32:13,728 --> 00:32:15,709
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in that sense, by being mindful of

419
00:32:17,246 --> 00:32:25,414
[SPEAKER_00]: Attitude of dispersion towards the body, you're mindful of attitude of dispersion towards the nature of the body.

420
00:32:31,079 --> 00:32:36,284
[SPEAKER_00]: And you can do that by, again, being mindful of the situation while you're looking at a Subha.

421
00:32:37,125 --> 00:32:38,967
[SPEAKER_00]: So, don't go fully look at a Subha.

422
00:32:39,147 --> 00:32:42,250
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, don't give 100% attention and forget which you are and what you're doing.

423
00:32:44,993 --> 00:32:48,315
[SPEAKER_00]: You're mindful of your situation, and then look at a surah.

424
00:32:50,296 --> 00:32:50,936
[SPEAKER_00]: And keep looking.

425
00:32:50,956 --> 00:32:53,358
[SPEAKER_00]: That's something you're doing, while you're mindful of the situation.

426
00:32:54,198 --> 00:32:54,498
[SPEAKER_00]: Within...

427
00:32:54,759 --> 00:32:59,721
[SPEAKER_00]: So, peripherally, you're aware of it, but you don't go full in it.

428
00:33:00,402 --> 00:33:10,588
[SPEAKER_00]: And then it... then it... As such, you start recognizing it, through that indirect attention, which is not

429
00:33:12,377 --> 00:33:18,498
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's indirect only in relation to what you're used to be with, what you're used to be direct.

430
00:33:19,098 --> 00:33:23,619
[SPEAKER_00]: It's only indirect in relation to that, but in itself, it's just a different form of attending.

431
00:33:25,399 --> 00:33:26,400
[SPEAKER_00]: Peripheral attending.

432
00:33:28,020 --> 00:33:31,160
[SPEAKER_00]: Without over-committing, without fully conceiving, without going there.

433
00:33:33,461 --> 00:33:39,862
[SPEAKER_00]: And that body, that dispassion that is manifested at that time, through that peripheral attending, is one of the bodies.

434
00:33:43,887 --> 00:33:44,848
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's one of the mantra bodies.

435
00:33:44,908 --> 00:33:45,808
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't require you.

436
00:33:47,189 --> 00:33:48,210
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't require mind.

437
00:33:49,111 --> 00:33:50,112
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't require doing it.

438
00:33:55,696 --> 00:33:56,877
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you've done something.

439
00:33:57,918 --> 00:33:58,938
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's all to do that.

440
00:34:00,379 --> 00:34:06,364
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you just have to start recognizing it, without taking it up fully.

441
00:34:08,065 --> 00:34:11,608
[SPEAKER_00]: And you'll make sure you won't take it up fully, for as long as you remain mindful.

442
00:34:12,338 --> 00:34:13,078
[SPEAKER_00]: What about, eh...

443
00:34:44,502 --> 00:34:46,763
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you can look at awareness, like awareness.

444
00:34:47,683 --> 00:34:48,464
[SPEAKER_00]: That's situation.

445
00:34:49,184 --> 00:34:49,944
[SPEAKER_01]: What situation?

446
00:34:50,044 --> 00:34:51,425
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, look yourself.

447
00:34:51,845 --> 00:34:54,186
[SPEAKER_00]: My awareness, that's basically my situation.

448
00:34:55,227 --> 00:34:57,508
[SPEAKER_00]: General awareness without anybody, that's my situation.

449
00:34:58,248 --> 00:35:09,053
[SPEAKER_00]: Obviously, just dwelling in my general awareness, well, that becomes something you actually do, and it becomes a particular thing, which means then the background of it would be something else.

450
00:35:10,253 --> 00:35:13,575
[SPEAKER_00]: So, no, you want to take up situation in regard to something.

451
00:35:15,072 --> 00:35:29,203
[SPEAKER_00]: In regard to your body, in regard to your feelings, in regard to your mind, for that matter, which is almost like a situation, or in regard to the thoughts that arise, false adhipatānas.

452
00:35:35,808 --> 00:35:43,875
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you become peripherally aware of your body within, that's important, within,

453
00:35:44,805 --> 00:35:46,426
[SPEAKER_00]: That situation is your mind.

454
00:35:49,227 --> 00:35:56,130
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, even if you forget about your situation, the fact that that body is still there, that can become your anchor.

455
00:35:58,130 --> 00:35:59,851
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you get anchored through the anchor.

456
00:36:00,591 --> 00:36:02,092
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how mindfulness progresses.

457
00:36:04,613 --> 00:36:05,273
[SPEAKER_00]: Or expands.

458
00:36:07,134 --> 00:36:08,755
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you particularly think you have another body?

459
00:36:10,956 --> 00:36:13,757
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, then, yeah, then this body out there,

460
00:36:15,225 --> 00:36:16,945
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, that becomes your situation.

461
00:36:19,066 --> 00:36:25,968
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means, you don't have to do anything, for as long as your body is just out there, your situation is out there, and you're mindful.

462
00:36:26,268 --> 00:36:28,268
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it doesn't require any attention.

463
00:36:29,809 --> 00:36:35,470
[SPEAKER_00]: Because attention means attending something, which means whenever you attend something, there is peripheral.

464
00:36:36,850 --> 00:36:38,211
[SPEAKER_00]: There is actual, there is peripheral.

465
00:36:40,431 --> 00:36:40,691
[SPEAKER_00]: Always.

466
00:36:40,931 --> 00:36:42,552
[SPEAKER_00]: Even if you give a hundred percent,

467
00:36:43,403 --> 00:36:45,184
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is actually possible, as you can see.

468
00:36:46,924 --> 00:36:52,546
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't, like, give 100% of your attention to something, because that would mean you're fully absorbed in that thing.

469
00:36:53,186 --> 00:36:56,567
[SPEAKER_00]: But there is always a background to whatever you're fully attending.

470
00:36:57,627 --> 00:37:01,268
[SPEAKER_00]: And that background is always something that you're peripherally aware of.

471
00:37:02,729 --> 00:37:04,089
[SPEAKER_00]: That's just how things are ordered.

472
00:37:04,109 --> 00:37:05,750
[SPEAKER_00]: That's just the nature of the aggregates.

473
00:37:07,290 --> 00:37:09,471
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when you fully develop that knowledge,

474
00:37:11,300 --> 00:37:13,281
[SPEAKER_00]: Means you can be fully attending whatever you want.

475
00:37:13,781 --> 00:37:15,002
[SPEAKER_00]: Your mindfulness cannot latch.

476
00:37:15,842 --> 00:37:16,042
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

477
00:37:16,082 --> 00:37:17,623
[SPEAKER_00]: Because there is always spiritual awareness.

478
00:37:18,083 --> 00:37:19,024
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's fully known.

479
00:37:19,924 --> 00:37:21,865
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why consciousness is to be understood.

480
00:37:23,926 --> 00:37:25,247
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the direction of consciousness.

481
00:37:25,667 --> 00:37:28,368
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that's the way.

482
00:37:28,448 --> 00:37:40,434
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's the... way to abandon...

483
00:37:43,859 --> 00:38:05,098
[SPEAKER_00]: It means that no matter how raging your body is, in terms of anger, or lust, or whatever else, well, now you learn how to see it indirectly.

484
00:38:05,118 --> 00:38:08,722
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, seeing it indirectly means seeing it as not mine.

485
00:38:12,267 --> 00:38:14,687
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, there's a cold cut, kind of.

486
00:38:15,668 --> 00:38:17,668
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can choose to go into it.

487
00:38:18,008 --> 00:38:18,508
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

488
00:38:18,528 --> 00:38:19,228
[SPEAKER_01]: You know you can.

489
00:38:19,428 --> 00:38:26,170
[SPEAKER_00]: Unless when you become an anāgāmī, and then an arahant, whereby even the choice of going back into it is fully understood.

490
00:38:26,870 --> 00:38:29,810
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, even going back into it becomes inconceivable.

491
00:38:29,830 --> 00:38:30,370
[SPEAKER_00]: The choices.

492
00:38:30,450 --> 00:38:31,911
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, because of sensuality and anger.

493
00:38:32,291 --> 00:38:34,131
[SPEAKER_00]: But they still have that, you know, the subtle.

494
00:38:34,511 --> 00:38:36,972
[SPEAKER_00]: Claiming for presence, claiming for non-presence, and so on.

495
00:38:37,832 --> 00:38:38,392
[SPEAKER_00]: For absence.

496
00:38:44,987 --> 00:38:46,848
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it that the self is on the general level?

497
00:38:47,908 --> 00:38:50,108
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, self is usually where you don't look.

498
00:38:53,589 --> 00:38:56,730
[SPEAKER_00]: But, yes, self never appears as an object which you can look at.

499
00:38:56,790 --> 00:39:08,514
[SPEAKER_00]: However, if you learn how to see things peripherally, then the general sense of self is seen peripherally, as such.

500
00:39:09,174 --> 00:39:11,895
[SPEAKER_00]: But it has to... And, as I said, it's within the situation.

501
00:39:12,215 --> 00:39:13,575
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything is within the situation.

502
00:39:14,660 --> 00:39:16,281
[SPEAKER_01]: It eventually appears in some.

503
00:39:16,781 --> 00:39:19,263
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it always appears in that negative manner.

504
00:39:20,163 --> 00:39:28,928
[SPEAKER_00]: But the whole peripheral, the whole prospect of the peripheral, is a negative in regard to what you're used to looking in front of you, which is positive.

505
00:39:29,909 --> 00:39:32,090
[SPEAKER_00]: But there is always a degree of negative in regard to everything.

506
00:39:32,710 --> 00:39:35,812
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is why there's always a degree of self-perpetuation in regard to everything.

507
00:39:40,857 --> 00:39:53,624
[SPEAKER_00]: But once you start abandoning actual emptiness, as mind, then that which used to be your Self, well, those things still keep manifesting, but now they are not mind.

508
00:39:54,404 --> 00:39:56,405
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, there is no more Self of mind.

509
00:40:08,432 --> 00:40:10,113
[SPEAKER_01]: If I try to find the Self and then

510
00:40:12,068 --> 00:40:14,330
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, you can't find it.

511
00:40:14,650 --> 00:40:22,797
[SPEAKER_00]: You can discern the phenomenon that's mine, that's me, that's I am, within the general situation.

512
00:40:26,860 --> 00:40:32,805
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, for another one, that just becomes like a shape of individual that he is.

513
00:40:33,566 --> 00:40:38,370
[SPEAKER_00]: Phenomenological shape of there used to be me, mine, now it's just this individual.

514
00:40:54,977 --> 00:41:04,922
[SPEAKER_01]: But things are establishments of mind, then, or something you do better, or you can do better.

515
00:41:07,836 --> 00:41:22,243
[SPEAKER_00]: While being mindful of the situation, while having that proper attentional peripheral... Yeah, that's the direction for any establishment of mind, whether jhānas or anything, the Sīla practice, it's that, through that development of that peripheral.

516
00:41:22,963 --> 00:41:32,068
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, because once you have that established, then you can establish other things, other particular things, like compassion or whatever, kindness.

517
00:41:33,845 --> 00:41:34,545
[SPEAKER_00]: I see what you mean.

518
00:41:34,565 --> 00:41:35,706
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, yeah, yeah.

519
00:41:35,846 --> 00:41:38,086
[SPEAKER_00]: You can be dwelling in it more particularly.

520
00:41:39,927 --> 00:41:42,007
[SPEAKER_01]: You can take a particular perception.

521
00:41:42,047 --> 00:41:42,747
[SPEAKER_00]: Literally, yeah.

522
00:41:44,448 --> 00:41:47,989
[SPEAKER_01]: To help undo things more, more faster.

523
00:41:48,789 --> 00:41:59,612
[SPEAKER_00]: Because when you're established in the jhāna situation, you realize, okay, now I'm beyond griefs and joys in regard to the world.

524
00:42:05,634 --> 00:42:20,419
[SPEAKER_00]: When you're in the state of that beyond, then, well, now I might as well, since you can, make that body which is not mine, which is already there, on its own, think things that are good for it, such as compassion and everything else.

525
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:33,023
[SPEAKER_00]: So then, when I'm not mindful, if I fall back, lapse, forget, get careless, fall back into the more wholesome environment that I might appropriate again as mine,

526
00:42:33,802 --> 00:42:39,827
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you keep doing it, you keep doing it, you keep doing it, until eventually, for an hour, you can't even fall back anymore.

527
00:42:41,348 --> 00:42:42,188
[SPEAKER_00]: It's fully developed.

528
00:42:44,890 --> 00:42:49,834
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is how you can operate and exist like every other living being.

529
00:42:50,434 --> 00:42:52,316
[SPEAKER_00]: And you can't tell the difference externally.

530
00:42:59,761 --> 00:43:00,522
[SPEAKER_00]: Could it be the Buddha?

531
00:43:04,815 --> 00:43:07,358
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes people didn't recognize him.

532
00:43:07,378 --> 00:43:11,881
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes people, they were his followers, like that monk, who never met him.

533
00:43:12,722 --> 00:43:13,223
[SPEAKER_00]: In the bar?

534
00:43:13,243 --> 00:43:13,823
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

535
00:43:14,063 --> 00:43:16,165
[SPEAKER_00]: In the bar, yeah, and they spent like ten years recognizing him.

536
00:43:16,566 --> 00:43:17,066
[SPEAKER_00]: How could he?

537
00:43:18,908 --> 00:43:25,253
[SPEAKER_00]: How could anybody, short of a Buddha, or an Arahant at least, or from... with great powers, recognize him?

538
00:43:25,273 --> 00:43:25,654
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't.

539
00:43:26,935 --> 00:43:28,636
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's nothing to do with external anyone.

540
00:43:29,997 --> 00:43:30,538
[SPEAKER_01]: Or very little.

541
00:43:32,962 --> 00:43:41,730
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, I saw this whole story about the description of how the Buddha's body was... Oh, yeah, it was in the 13... 32 or 36 months, yeah, I don't remember.

542
00:43:43,171 --> 00:43:51,379
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, but it's hard to decide for that, because it just... it was like in every Indian religion, they have its... Yeah, the birth story.

543
00:43:51,419 --> 00:43:51,959
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

544
00:43:52,019 --> 00:43:53,240
[SPEAKER_01]: And all sorts.

545
00:43:53,320 --> 00:43:54,241
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's irrelevant.

546
00:43:54,441 --> 00:43:55,783
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

547
00:43:55,803 --> 00:43:58,325
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing to do with anything of significance.

548
00:44:01,453 --> 00:44:12,782
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, the first person the Buddha met upon his enlightenment, when he saw, oh, wow, look, this monk is quite bright, his senses are clear, confidently walking, he looks like he might be enlightened.

549
00:44:12,842 --> 00:44:14,083
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he kind of suspected.

550
00:44:14,724 --> 00:44:19,228
[SPEAKER_00]: This is quite a confident look the Buddha was emitting, like a great lion.

551
00:44:19,848 --> 00:44:23,191
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he asked him, ah, whose, whose, whose instruction did you follow?

552
00:44:24,292 --> 00:44:24,972
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, no one.

553
00:44:25,052 --> 00:44:26,373
[SPEAKER_00]: I, I enlightened myself.

554
00:44:26,413 --> 00:44:27,674
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm fully enlightened by myself.

555
00:44:27,734 --> 00:44:28,675
[SPEAKER_00]: Nobody is my teacher.

556
00:44:28,755 --> 00:44:30,337
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm my own dharma, the supreme leader.

557
00:44:31,313 --> 00:44:34,175
[SPEAKER_00]: And what happens when I say, yeah, right, so be it.

558
00:44:34,335 --> 00:44:34,655
Yeah.

559
00:44:34,996 --> 00:44:36,237
[SPEAKER_00]: Laugh at him who walked off.

560
00:44:38,138 --> 00:44:39,659
[SPEAKER_01]: He'll beat you drunk.

561
00:44:41,761 --> 00:44:43,322
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, and that's what the Buddha realized.

562
00:44:43,422 --> 00:44:50,127
[SPEAKER_00]: Ah, if he, if he, if he approaches this, because he could have said, yeah, I'm the greatest man in the world, because it will be factual.

563
00:44:50,827 --> 00:44:54,129
[SPEAKER_00]: He's the greatest in, like, every realm.

564
00:44:54,570 --> 00:44:55,430
[SPEAKER_00]: Not just this world.

565
00:44:56,771 --> 00:44:58,513
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the extent of being the Buddha.

566
00:44:58,553 --> 00:44:59,193
[SPEAKER_00]: So there was that.

567
00:44:59,533 --> 00:45:00,274
[SPEAKER_00]: He could have said that.

568
00:45:01,424 --> 00:45:01,904
[SPEAKER_00]: It wouldn't be a lie.

569
00:45:01,924 --> 00:45:02,724
[SPEAKER_00]: It wouldn't be conceit.

570
00:45:02,744 --> 00:45:03,685
[SPEAKER_00]: It wouldn't be nothing like that.

571
00:45:04,505 --> 00:45:15,208
[SPEAKER_00]: But because everybody else is clouded by their conceit, they could have not possibly seen it as anything other than conceit, which is exactly what this man... Oh, really?

572
00:45:15,228 --> 00:45:15,508
